  "goodToKnow": "Die Neuzeit is the modern era in history, which German historians date from around 1500, after das Mittelalter (Middle Ages). Its start is linked to Gutenberg's printing press, Columbus's voyage in 1492 and Luther's Reformation of 1517. Die Frühe Neuzeit is the early modern period, up to about 1800. Die Neuzeit is a fixed historical term; for modern times in general, Germans say die Moderne or die Gegenwart."
